{
  "comment": "Upstream code compiled as it is from part of a file whose rest is bound to the VCL GUI (ADR 0014, amendment P3-06d). Each slice is the lines from the one line matching 'from' up to the one matching 'until' (or the file's end), taken from the transformed file ('transformed': true; the file must be in the transform's scope) or the pristine one, after a linscp prologue (and before an epilogue, when one is given), with #line so diagnostics name upstream's lines. Anchors must each match exactly once: a pin bump that moves or changes them fails the transform instead of cutting the wrong code.",
  "slices": [
    {
      "output": "windows/CustomCommandType.h",
      "source": "source/windows/WinConfiguration.h",
      "transformed": true,
      "prologue": [
        "#pragma once",
        "#include \"CustomCommandsSlice.h\""
      ],
      "from": "^class TCustomCommandType\\s*$",
      "until": "^extern TWinConfiguration \\* WinConfiguration;"
    },
    {
      "output": "windows/CustomCommandType.cpp",
